# `fluid::Action`

A change to one pump or one valve.

## Signature

```cpp
fluid::Action
```

## What It Does

Names a device and what to do to it. It is carried by a `TimeControl` or a `StateControl`.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `device` | Pump or valve. | Pump |
| `index` | The pump or valve index within its family. | 0 |
| `act` | Open, Close or Set. | Open |
| `value` | The speed, loss coefficient, flow or pressure head for `Set`. | 0 |

## Returns

A value.

## Errors

An index outside the family and an invalid `value` are rejected by `run`.

## Interpretation and Use

Aggregate-initialise it: `{fluid::Device::Pump, 0, fluid::Act::Set, 0.7}`. The meaning of `value` follows the device and, for a valve, its kind.

